WEBVTT

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.940
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.280
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.990
but also in crime.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.240
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.660
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.830
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:49.520
moshimo ima anata no yume no eria ga
Should the area of your dreams

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.070
namida ni okasare
Be invaded now by tears

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:01.620
kujiketa toki wa nee kokoro de
When I faltered, in my heart

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:08.040
watashi no namae yonde
My name calls

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.300
hurry up hurry up ai no tsubasa
Hurry up, hurry up, the wings of love

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:20.010
anata no sora e tonde yuku
Will fly to your sky

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.140
I’m gonna fly fly away

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.140
KONDISHON GUURIN
Condition green

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:33.230
mukai kanashimi wo tasuketai no
Do you want to help this deep sorrow?

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:36.240
Just fly fly away

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:42.660
onaji itami wo mune no REDAA wa
The radar of your heart

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:48.080
itsu demo kanjite iru wa
Is always feeling the same pain

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:54.420
Just I'm gonna fly away

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:01.390
I'm Selling Peace of Mind

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:18.990
He's too much for us to handle.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.660
Watch out!
He's firing a rocket!

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:39.130
Good move, Ota!

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.140
It takes skill!

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.010
Or just brute strength.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.060
What did you say?

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.100
He's getting away.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:49.810
Come on, Ota.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.240
Stop!
Stop or I'll shoot!

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.080
Wait!
Watch out for the cars!

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.000
Take this!

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.100
How dare you resist arrest!

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.030
We need to reenact
the whole incident?

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.110
Yes.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:42.360
Why on earth do we
have to do that?

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.620
Because of the parked
cars Ota trampled.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.450
Our insurance
company insists on it.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:58.880
They're worried about how
many claims we've been filing.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:03.470
But why? We've never
had to do this before!

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:06.140
We already told them everything.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:09.560
Aren't we covered for any
accident in the line of duty?

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:10.560
Listen -

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:14.020
Well why do we
have insurance then?

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:18.770
That's right! Our insurance was
designed to cover Patlabors.

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:21.360
That's why it's so expensive!

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.990
So why do we need
some stupid reenactment?

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:27.410
Hey, it isn't <i>your</i> money.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:28.490
What?

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:29.660
Anyway...

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:33.710
they've already scheduled
us all for the walk-through.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.420
All of us?

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:36.540
That's right.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:50.810
We don't have all day.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:57.020
But we need an
exact re-creation.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:00.690
Then we'll need full
access to the site.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:03.900
But they're in the
middle of construction.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.070
I wish we didn't
have to do this.

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.550
I'm so sorry I'm late.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:30.510
I'm Naoyo Yamada, the
inspector assigned to this claim.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:31.930
Where's the captain?

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:33.020
Over there.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:53.540
So this is where you
pulled him to a stop.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:57.500
I attempted to stop the
criminal as quickly as possible.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:02.000
Yes, I'm sure you're
very diligent in your duty.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.500
Of course!

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:06.840
Still, his exit was blocked
by the Labor carrier.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:11.010
I'm sure you were
driving him back carefully.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:11.800
Well, uh...

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:16.730
Good.
We just need to confirm it.

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:19.650
Let's move to the
scene of the capture.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:23.270
Miss Izumi, you can
stand in for the villain.

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.240
The villain?

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:36.910
Why do I have to
be the bad guy?

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.430
And this is where the cars were.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:51.050
All right, please begin.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.430
Remember, this isn't for real.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.220
Of course.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.650
I used full speed to
close the distance.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.360
Stop!
Stop!

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:14.490
And then?

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:18.450
Once I was sure I had him
stopped, I pulled back.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:29.630
No pivoting of the leg.
How many seconds did that take?

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.340
Three or four.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:36.810
Yes, that's about right.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:43.730
Mr. Ota, your recorders say you
lifted the target for 0.8 seconds.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:45.770
Would you do that, too?

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:47.570
Roger.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:14.050
Car B

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:17.300
Thank you.
That will do fine.

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:20.890
That was too rough!

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:29.270
Thank you. I appreciate
the use of your equipment.

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:31.490
Oh, no problem.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:36.620
I have no feel for machines.
The reports don't tell me enough.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:39.200
But now I have a better idea.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.120
I have a bit of a
feel for Miss Ingra.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:43.370
Miss Ingra?

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:47.670
Sorry. It's easier to remember if
I give the machines nicknames.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.290
If you don't mind, I'd...

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:54.510
The main office will make their
decision and contact you soon.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:04.560
What a waste of time!
After all our hard work...

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:07.350
it's still up to the
insurance company!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:09.310
That's the way it always works.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:11.860
Why won't our premiums go down?

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:17.280
They'd like to prove negligence,
so they don't have to pay.

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:19.660
How can we do our job...

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:21.240
if we have to worry
about insurance?

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:26.710
But we couldn't do our
job without insurance.

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:28.880
Are you one of their paid spies?

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.250
Of course not!

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:33.710
I won't be beaten by a
bunch of bean counters!

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:37.010
Ota, want any tea?

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:41.050
I've grown too complacent
about destruction.

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:42.680
I won't disagree.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:43.390
You think so?

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:46.850
Your insurance claims are
eight times higher than ours.

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:51.320
I suspected that,
but... eight times?

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.450
Our new dictator has arrived.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:07.910
I think Ota is right.

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:11.420
He's a good officer, but he can't
see anything except his target.

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:16.840
Fancy meeting you here!

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:22.550
About our claim...

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:28.730
Let me explain. Patlabor
insurance is highly specialized.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:34.610
The conditions of a claim are
nearly impossible to reproduce...

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:42.200
so I've been asked to accompany
you, until another accident occurs.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.370
I apologize for
the inconvenience.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:49.920
Now let's get back to work.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:07.850
Say...

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:10.440
Where did everyone go?

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.980
I don't know!
I'm going to the restroom.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.110
Take your time.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:21.950
Washroom

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:23.530
Well?

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:25.620
I don't think she suspects.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:29.160
I'm against it!
It's misuse of official funds!

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:33.210
Not that. How can we sway
Judge Judy out there?

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:36.920
Just flatter her.
Pile on the compliments!

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:40.420
She <i>does</i> have
discretionary authority.

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.430
We have no choice.

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:50.100
Use our best tea.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:51.310
I know.

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.440
Does this look about right?

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:08.740
Up close, it's really quite
an impressive machine.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:44.200
I know it's hard to work
with a stranger underfoot.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:47.120
Thanks for giving me a desk.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:47.780
It's nothing.

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:49.910
And you have such a hard job.

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:54.580
It's my chosen career, so
I've never thought of it as hard.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:57.420
You're an amazing man, Ota.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.340
I'm nothing special.

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:04.090
Despite all my work on this case,
the main office is stubborn.

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:10.060
Insurance should be there to
help people like you, Mr. Ota.

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:12.430
All done!

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:14.180
Thank you very much!

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.400
Oh, this tea is quite excellent!

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:22.780
Really?

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:27.990
Have you seen that
insurance adjuster?

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:30.280
I wish they'd sent
somebody younger.

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:32.330
What a cushy job.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.330
Watch your mouths.

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:39.920
Her report means a lot to us,
so be careful what you say.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:41.800
Oh, I see!

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:44.380
Why are you looking
at me like that?

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:47.380
Don't get any ideas!

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:51.810
She's the one who insisted
on sewing up my shirt.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:57.020
Such trivialities won't change
my opinion about our insurance.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:59.060
But it doesn't hurt
that she's so nice.

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:02.520
Maybe you're starting
to see her point of view.

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:04.650
Don't start imagining things!

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.240
Tea's ready.

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:12.950
Well then, let's eat.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.540
That looks fabulous!

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.710
I wasn't sure you'd like this.

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:20.670
This took a lot of time!

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.380
Oh, it's no harder
than cooking for one.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:26.340
You don't have to go
out of your way for us.

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:31.140
Oh, not at all. It's important
for me to see how you all work.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:32.970
Of course, but...

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:36.560
Where's Ota?

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:38.310
I'll go get him.

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:45.730
I seem to have upset
Mr. Ota somehow.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.080
Ota!

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.290
What are you doing here?

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:01.540
What does it look like?
I'm eating.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:05.750
Ms. Yamada brought lunch.
Don't you want to eat with us?

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:09.090
We shouldn't get too chummy.
She and I both have work to do.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:12.930
You worry too much
about formalities, Ota.

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:17.930
Does anyone care that she
isn't part of the force?

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:23.100
What about lunch?

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:24.860
We'll eat it later!

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:30.820
What a job! They don't
even have time for lunch.

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:38.540
A terrorist group has stolen a
heavy-duty Labor and its carrier.

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:43.250
Fortunately, the carrier had
a location transponder.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.750
We'll ambush them
at Ichinoe, Loop 7.

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:50.800
How can you ambush them
in the middle of Tokyo traffic?

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:53.970
First, we're sending
in unmarked cars.

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:08.820
<i>In pursuit. Please fall back.</i>

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:25.460
As they near the ambush,
patrol cars will pull in front.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:38.600
We've blocked the opposite lanes,
so we'll intercept them here.

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:53.700
We can pull this off because
of the location transponder.

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:55.110
It's real-time.

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:06.000
Now.

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:12.130
That's far enough!

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:26.730
Operation complete.

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:42.080
Ota, pull in the back
end of the trailer.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:43.750
Roger.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:12.480
Perhaps insuring Patlabors was
just a bad idea in the first place.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:13.320
Good point.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.000
This area's off limits.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.330
Let me through!
I have to get my bike.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:36.550
I hope Ms. Yamada isn't mad.

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:38.050
Please, don't remind me.

00:18:57.530 --> 00:19:00.160
Your policy doesn't
cover that bike.

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:01.660
Of course not.

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:11.210
You wrecked my bike!
You're so mean!

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:30.730
Isao Ota
Division 2

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:33.690
There's no line
for an explanation.

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:36.110
It was entirely my fault.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.070
Uh...

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:38.940
What?

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:42.160
May I have permission
to leave the station?

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:49.290
A bike?

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:53.500
Yes. A woman stopped by from
the Patlabor insurance company.

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.340
I see.

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:59.710
An Ingram!
Cool!

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:02.630
Take that!
And that! And that!

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:06.300
What are you doing
to your new present?

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:10.350
This is what happened!

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:15.100
Thank you.
I'm sorry about this...

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:21.280
No, I'm the one
who should apologize.

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:25.870
Mister, you're so cool!

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:34.870
Ota, it's incredible!

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:40.460
They've renewed our coverage!

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:44.470
And all previous claims
have been approved!

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:45.680
Really?

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:49.760
Ms. Yamada pulled off a miracle!

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:51.430
Actually, she's the
company's director.

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:55.100
Apparently, she worked her
way up from the sales floor.

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:58.650
She said, "Charity is
a good investment."

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:05.570
You can't be serious!

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:14.750
May I speak to you?

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:17.460
Go on ahead.

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:22.170
About the bike...

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:27.720
You went to his house? How like
you, Mr. Ota. So responsible.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.800
I'll reimburse you.

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:32.640
Not at all. I took it out of
company expenses.

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:34.850
But...

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:42.820
You work so hard, I can't let you
be distracted by petty details.

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:45.610
I was just trying to help out.

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:49.120
Don't worry about it.

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:53.330
There must be some
way I can repay you!

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:57.170
Well, perhaps...

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:05.260
NOW, EVEN MORE DEVOTED TO DUTY

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:10.760
SAFETY FIRST!

00:22:10.760 --> 00:22:16.480
PROTECTED BY NEW LABOR DAMAGE INSURANCE

00:22:26.360 --> 00:22:28.700
I guess she can read
people pretty well.

00:22:28.700 --> 00:22:30.870
Ota, you're famous!

00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:34.870
How could I refuse?

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:35.950
How, indeed?

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:04.940
arashi ga itsushika owatta
When I looked out, the storm had passed a long time ago.

00:23:07.030 --> 00:23:12.700
yuube no kobushi wa kirei ni
The morning dew betrays how yesterday's...

00:23:12.620 --> 00:23:14.660
arawareta
sorrows have been washed away.

00:23:15.910 --> 00:23:20.120
yoake ga NEJI wo yurumereba
Dawn is let loose by unbolting the panels of night.

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:28.420
MASHIN ya BIRU ga mezameru
Even machines and the buildings all wake up.

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:30.680
I got it

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:38.220
tooku ga mieru yo PANORAMA mitai sa
Now I can see so far ahead, an unfolding panorama.

00:23:38.390 --> 00:23:44.110
doko kara mite mo heiwa-na Happy Island
Wherever I watch from, I see a peaceful, happy island.

00:23:44.230 --> 00:23:45.650
One more chance

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:53.280
kimi ni oshietai kimi ni tsutaetai
The thing I want to tell to you, the thing I want to show to you

00:23:53.410 --> 00:23:58.740
yume no GEITO ga me no mae de
The shining gate to our dreams lays open to us...

00:23:59.450 --> 00:24:02.420
ima hiraku yo
right now before our eyes.

00:24:07.920 --> 00:24:11.920
This story is fiction...

00:24:07.920 --> 00:24:11.920
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:18.390 --> 00:24:20.930
Division 2 has found an
underground dungeon!

00:24:20.930 --> 00:24:24.810
It's an old garbage disposal passage!
It's dark and cold and stinky!

00:24:24.810 --> 00:24:26.560
Hey, for a summertime
adventure, it's great!

00:24:26.560 --> 00:24:27.980
And if we find any treasure
we'll divide it up evenly.

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:29.860
Asuma, do you
believe in astrology?

00:24:29.860 --> 00:24:34.280
My horoscope says items that
are white and the #4 are bad luck!

00:24:34.280 --> 00:24:34.910
So what?

00:24:34.910 --> 00:24:36.870
I have a bad feeling the
unlucky stuff is down there.

